    {
      "id": "x1zo9un",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. LUCKNOW PACT (1916)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Lucknow Pact (1916) brought the Indian National Congress and Muslim League onto a joint political platform.",
        "The Simon Commission (1927) was met with widespread boycotts due to the total exclusion of Indian members.",
        "The Lahore Session (1929) passed the historic 'Purna Swaraj' (Complete Independence) resolution.",
        "The Poona Pact (1932) replaced separate electorates for depressed classes with reserved seats within general electorates.",
        "The Mountbatten Plan (1947) laid out the final framework for the partition of British India and transfer of power."
      ],
      "id": "67tkwrh"
    },
